<title>USA: AMC Entertainment sells 144A notes.</title>
<headline>AMC Entertainment sells 144A notes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following 144A issue from AMC Entertainment was priced in the private placement market on Friday via co-lead managers Goldman Sachs &amp; Co Inc and Salomon Brothers, according to market sources. AMC currently owns and operates 230 movie theaters with 1,930 screens around the world.</p>
<p>BORROWER AMC ENTERTAINMENT INC</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 9.50 PCT   MATURITY 3/15/2009</p>
<p>TYPE SNR SUB NOTES ISS PRICE 99.469  FIRST PAY DATE 9/15/1997 LAST MOODY'S B2    YIELD 9.575 PCT   PAY FREQ SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-B  SPREAD 287.5	CALLABLE NON-CALL FIVE</p>
<p>((--U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212 859-1678))</p>
</text>
